{
 "_provenance": {
  "captured": "2026-08-04",
  "why": "A Kalshi event whose NESTED markets carry DIFFERING close_times and DIFFERING statuses. prediction_market_venue_payloads.json's multi-market event shares one close_time across its nested markets, so it cannot distinguish the event-level close_time = max(nested) derivation from the old nested[0] read, nor is_resolved = all(nested resolved) from nested[0]'s status. KXMARRIAGESTYLESKRAVITZ-HSZK pins both at once: four distinct close_times, and nested[0] is `finalized` while the other three are `active`, so a nested[0] read reports the event RESOLVED and closing 18 months early. Measured on the frozen universe, nested[0] misclassifies ~305 live event families as RESOLVED.",
  "endpoints": {
   "kalshi": "https://api.elections.kalshi.com/trade-api/v2/events?status=open&limit=200&with_nested_markets=true"
  },
  "edits": "Two events lifted verbatim from one live page of the free unauthenticated /events endpoint; string values over 300 chars truncated. No key was renamed, added or removed - key PRESENCE and the full ~38-key market shape are what the projection test asserts against (it must prove the unlisted keys are DROPPED, which a pre-projected fixture could not show). `cursor` is blanked so a handler serving this as an /events page terminates pagination instead of looping.",
  "events": {
   "KXMARRIAGESTYLESKRAVITZ-HSZK": "4 nested markets, 4 distinct close_times (2026-07-01 .. 2028-01-01), nested[0] status=finalized and the rest active. Event-level settlement_sources populated; every market-level copy is null.",
   "USCLIMATE": "2 nested markets, 2 distinct close_times, all active (is_resolved=False), and a single real EPA settlement source - a joinable epa.gov registrable domain for the settlement-join channel."
  }
 },
